# Omarchy base packages left out of the SM-T715 arm64 image on purpose.
#
# The image installs Omarchy's own list, install/omarchy-base.packages of the
# installed omarchy package, minus the names below. One name per line,
# "name  # reason"; the reason is copied into the MANIFEST. Names of Omarchy's
# list that no aarch64 repository serves (the AUR ones, and those Omarchy
# publishes for x86_64 only) are left out automatically and listed in the
# MANIFEST as unavailable, so they need no line here.
# Adapted from omarchy-tab-s2/image/rootfs/packages.omarchy-skip.

# --- Heavy desktop applications: not needed by the session or the shell ---
libreoffice-fresh       # office suite, the biggest package of the list
kdenlive                # video editor
obs-studio              # screen recording and streaming (not in the aarch64 repositories either)
xournalpp               # handwritten notes
moonlight-qt            # game streaming client
gpu-screen-recorder     # needs VAAPI/NVENC/Vulkan encoders; none on Mali-T760

# --- Containers: no container runtime in this test image ---
docker                  # Omarchy's setup would enable docker.socket
docker-buildx           # Docker plugin
docker-compose          # Docker plugin
lazydocker              # Docker TUI, useless without docker
ufw-docker              # ufw rules for Docker; depends on docker

# --- Toolchains, interpreters and database client libraries ---
clang                   # C/C++ toolchain
llvm                    # LLVM toolchain (mesa only needs llvm-libs, which stays)
ruby                    # Ruby interpreter
tobi-try                # Omarchy's "try" helper, written in Ruby: would pull ruby back in
luarocks                # Lua package manager
lua51                   # Lua 5.1 for luarocks/Neovim plugins, not used by the session
mariadb-libs            # MariaDB client library
postgresql-libs         # PostgreSQL client library

# --- OCR ---
tesseract               # OCR engine (Omarchy's screenshot-to-text)
tesseract-data-eng      # OCR language data

# --- Printing: no printer on a tablet test image ---
cups                    # print server
cups-filters            # print filters
cups-pk-helper          # polkit helper for CUPS
system-config-printer   # printer settings GUI

# --- Fonts ---
noto-fonts-cjk          # CJK glyphs, several hundred MiB

# --- Build-machine helpers ---
kernel-modules-hook     # keeps the running kernel's modules across upgrades; this image has no kernel and no modules
qemu-user-static-binfmt # runs other architectures' binaries: a build machine's job, not a tablet's

# --- arm64 port: power management is the kernel's (the rule of docs/hardware/CPUFREQ.md on frequencies and voltages) ---
power-profiles-daemon   # would switch CPU power profiles from Omarchy's Battery saver tile: nothing in this image may scale a frequency or a voltage

# --- New in Omarchy 4.5's list (2026-11-24), left out as the owner's Lenovomarchy
# --- port leaves them out (its image/rootfs/packages.omarchy-skip, M4-IMAGE-BUILD.md)
base-devel              # a compiler toolchain nobody uses on a touch tablet (~250 MiB); migration 1790702362 is held for the same reason
dotnet-runtime          # .NET runtime for apps the image does not install
fcitx5-chewing          # CJK input engines (~1 GiB together): squeekboard is the input method, there is no hardware keyboard (migration 1791367434 held)
fcitx5-chinese-addons   # CJK input engine (see fcitx5-chewing)
fcitx5-hangul           # CJK input engine (see fcitx5-chewing)
fcitx5-mozc             # CJK input engine (see fcitx5-chewing)
fcitx5-table-extra      # CJK input engine (see fcitx5-chewing)
